ssing data.\n- **Voluntary Participation:** Enrollment was voluntary, and early participants may have had more time to complete forms, potentially skewing the results.\n- **Survey Limitations:** The internal survey collected 87 responses, but it was not representative of all residents due to the inability to identify households that moved during the pilot.\n- **Training and Setup Costs:** Training and translation were the most significant initial setup costs, with recurring staff time expected to be more important in a larger rollout.\n- **Budget Exclusions:** The budget excludes volunteer labor, building depreciation, and costs paid by partner organizations.\n- **Sensor Installation:** A proposal to install extra sensors was deferred due to procurement extending beyond the pilot period.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n- **Weekly Counts:** Staff must publish weekly counts of delayed service cases.\n- **Missing Data:** Record missing data and offer paper and telephone channels.\n- **Comparison:** The next review will compare the same calendar months to reduce seasonal confusion.\n- **Audit:** One member requested an independent audit, but another argued that the small sample size could not support such an expense yet.\n- **Service Preservation:** The decision preserves the existing service in neighborhoods that have not joined, and no resident is required to participate.","text_utf8_repaired":false,"token_ids":[14374,21517,315,279,8748,271,334,74846,25,1019,785,64229,9290,220,20,14833,6635,311,13036,279,4743,22289,4752,48017,17708,369,458,5107,2326,3951,13,1096,8894,686,2138,369,803,15817,821,4426,323,6358,11,438,1632,438,27020,14976,4714,10820,2337,279,17708,382,334,44220,21312,7379,819,25,1019,12,3070,57361,5362,46024,66963,220,16,19,23,5048,304,279,1156,2254,323,220,16,17,20,304,279,1537,2254,624,12,3070,62901,66963,400,17,23,11,20,19,23,11792,369,279,17708,382,334,16527,804,25,1019,12,3070,1043,24704,66963,21566,504,1378,2849,1033,5558,4152,311,264,2355,88129,11,6388,311,740